BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (SmartFileSystem emerged in the late 1990s Amiga ecosystem as an alternative to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (original OFS/FFS families. It sought improved directory performance, efficient use of hard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (disks and stronger resilience to interruption than conventional bitmap updates. The Amiga) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (community and AmigaOS 4 documentation recognise SmartFileSystem as a separate format) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 608.0 Tm (rather than a variant of the DOS0-DOS5 family.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (AmigaOS developer and distribution archives record versions, tools and source components) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (of SmartFileSystem, including object and transaction handling. SFS0 and SFS2 should not be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (presented as identical disk layouts. The historical source releases and operating-system) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 527.0 Tm (support tables are important for assessing actual on-media revisions and operational) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 510.0 Tm (limits.) Tj ET
