BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 676.0 Tm (SmartFileSystem designs aim to avoid lengthy validation of a normally interrupted volume) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 659.0 Tm (by controlling metadata commit state. This is not a promise of full user-data journalling) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 642.0 Tm (or immunity to corrupted sectors. SFS transaction semantics should be explained from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 625.0 Tm (source code and not conflated with ext3 JBD, ZFS transaction groups or NTFS $LogFile.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 595.0 Tm (Recovering an SFS volume requires a consistent root, valid object tree, allocation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 578.0 Tm (metadata and acceptable transaction state. One must validate the on-disk format variant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 561.0 Tm (and preserve all recoverable versions of metadata before mutation. Format-recognition) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.07 0.16 0.23 rg 1 0 0 1 50 544.0 Tm (success does not establish that a damaged filesystem can be safely rewritten.) Tj ET
